ok   callbacks run base class first, then subclass, then the action, then after callbacks
ok   only: limits a callback to the listed actions
ok   except: skips a callback for the listed actions
ok   a before callback that redirects halts the chain
ok   after callbacks run after the action
ok   render plain: sends text/plain
ok   render json: generates JSON with application/json
ok   render html: escapes a String but not a SafeString
ok   render content_type: overrides the default
ok   render with a template name goes through render_template
ok   render with two bodies is an ArgumentError
ok   head :no_content sends an empty body
ok   redirect_to with a symbolic status
ok   before_action { |c| c.head :forbidden } sends 403
ok   before_action { |c| c.redirect_to ..., status: :see_other } sends 303
ok   rescue_from(X) { |c, e| c.head :not_found } sends 404
ok   rescue_from with: handles the exception through run_callback
ok   rescue_from with a block receives the controller and the exception
ok   an exception without a handler propagates out of process
ok   an action that renders nothing raises MissingTemplate
ok   an unknown callback name raises UnknownCallback
ok   process runs from a stored route handler
ok   chain_for and rescues_for walk the class hierarchy
ok   Callback#applies? honours only and except
ok   status_code maps symbols and passes integers through
ok   a missing required param answers 400 Bad Request
ok   a client fault raised in an action answers 400 with its message, like a missing param
ok   a client fault after the action redirected drops only Location and Content-Disposition
ok   a client fault answered from an action logs one rejected-request line
ok   an exception the controller re-raises is not logged by it (ErrorPages logs it once)
ok   an app exception sharing a bare name with a framework one is still raised (500 path)
